    <briefdescription>
<para>Policy parameters that govern exponential-backoff retry behaviour. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>All delay values are in milliseconds. Instances are cheap to copy.</para>
<para>Example (bind/listen retry — 3 attempts with 100 ms base): <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">WireRetryPolicy<sp/>p;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">p.max_attempts<sp/><sp/><sp/>=<sp/>3;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">p.base_delay_ms<sp/><sp/>=<sp/>100;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">p.max_delay_ms<sp/><sp/><sp/>=<sp/>2000;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">p.multiplier<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>=<sp/>2.0;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">p.enable_jitter<sp/><sp/>=<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">true</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
